PROMETHEUS & GRAFANA (Monitoring & Alerting Scenarios)

These scenarios focus on real outages, noisy alerts, and observability gaps seen in production systems.

⸻

📊 Prometheus & Grafana – Real-World DevOps Scenarios
 1. Alerts are firing, but the application seems healthy. How do you handle false positives?
 2. CPU usage is normal, but response time is high. What metrics do you investigate?
 3. Prometheus is running out of disk space. How do you fix and prevent it?
 4. A new service is deployed, but metrics are missing. How do you troubleshoot?
 5. How do you design meaningful alerts instead of noisy ones?
 6. Grafana dashboards are slow to load. How do you optimize them?
 7. An alert fired, but no one responded. How do you improve alert routing?
 8. How do you monitor Kubernetes pod-level and service-level metrics?
 9. Metrics disappeared after a restart. How do you prevent data loss?
 10. How do you detect memory leaks using monitoring tools?
 11. How do you monitor external dependencies (APIs, DBs)?
 12. Prometheus scrape targets are down. How do you debug?
 13. How do you define SLIs, SLOs, and SLAs using Prometheus metrics?
 14. A production incident occurred, but metrics are insufficient. How do you improve observability?
 15. How do you secure Prometheus and Grafana in production?

